<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The Figma design's page ground (`background`, #0B0D0F) — the same value as
      NivoraColors.ground in lib/core/theme/tokens.dart, which is the only other place it is
      written down. These two have to agree: this one is the Android window before Flutter
      paints, that one is the first thing Flutter paints, and the seam between them is
      visible on every cold start. See drawable/launch_background.xml for what happened when
      they did not.
    -->
    <color name="nivora_ground">#0B0D0F</color>
    <!--
      The Flutter light theme's ground, NivoraColors.background — and it is #EEF0F8 now, not
      #FFF8F3. Two things moved and this had to move with them:

        1. The light palette was redrawn off the gold seed onto hue 262, so the canvas changed
           from a warm #FFF8F3 to the cool #EEF0F8. This file kept the old value and nothing
           failed, because a launch-window mismatch is a 200ms flash rather than an error.
        2. The app is themeMode.light now, so this colour is what EVERY phone sees at launch —
           values-night/ points here too rather than at the dark ground.

      The chain is one colour end to end: launcher plate, launch window, splash, first screen.
      If NivoraColors.background changes again, change this in the same commit.
    -->
    <color name="nivora_ground_light">#EEF0F8</color>

    <!-- theme_color from app/manifest.ts -->
    <color name="colorPrimary">#F6F4EF</color>
    <color name="navigationColor">#F6F4EF</color>
    <!-- background_color from app/manifest.ts -->
    <color name="backgroundColor">#F6F4EF</color>
    <!--
      The plate behind the adaptive launcher icon, referenced only by
      mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml and ic_launcher_round.xml.

      This was #1C2B45 when the icon was the old placeholder — a white house drawn on
      navy. The real logo (nivoralogo.png) inverts that: the N-house mark is a dark navy
      gradient, measured at roughly #0B1D33, so on a navy plate it all but disappears.
      Ivory is the ground the logo was drawn for, and it matches background_color and
      theme_color in app/manifest.ts, so the launcher icon and the app it opens agree.

      Regenerate the icon layers with: node scripts/gen-icons.mjs
    -->
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">#F6F4EF</color>
</resources>
